{
  "_": "A town dressed in what we own (dressing.gd; art targets docs/art/target/01-town and town-composition/town-b; docs/research/free-rts-kits.md: use more of the Quaternius Fantasy Props, Village and Stylized Nature MegaKits). on: the switch (or --dressing=on / --dressing=off). kits: where each kit's models are (%s the model's name, every %s of it; meshy: a nature-set piece in its own folder) and the metres-to-world scale. trades.<trade>: what stands at that trade's building, each [kit/model, along (metres along its front, + to its right as you face it), out (metres out from its middle toward the street; the front wall is at about half the building's depth), turn (degrees), scale]. A thing is set down only where it blocks nothing: off every building, wall and stall (footprints), clear of every door (door), of the main streets (street) and back lanes (lane) from their middle, and of every work spot people stand at (spot), all in world units. homes: at a house's door, planters and flower boxes against its front, either side of the door ([kit/model, along, out, turn, scale], the door's own middle at along 0), by chance by rank. ground: between the houses, so the trodden ground isn't bare: tries a town by rank, each a pick from pick ([kit/model, weight, [smallest, largest] scale]), set down only where it blocks nothing, and kept apart (gap, world units). square_fronts: each house facing the square (its doorstep within reach of square_r) takes, by chance, one set against its front wall beside its door, squared to it, picked by weight: a bench, the shop's stores (barrels and crates), flower tubs, a barrel rack; each row [kit/model, along, out, turn, scale] as homes' (Mac on Kingsmere's square, 2026-11-12: benches and crates strewn at random angles over the paving read as riot debris; Anno 1800's and Manor Lords' streets: stock and seats against the walls, the walk left open). Nothing is dressed out on the square's paving: the market's own goods are towns.gd's piles at the stalls' ends and the fronts. rank: towns by rank (crown, seat, town, village) take this share of ground tries and homes' planters. Each model is drawn as one batch per town. What people walk over and walk round is read off each model's height (towns.json nav.tall, nav_ground.gd). clusters (docs/research/quality-deep-dive.md #4, Anno's 1-2 / few / many): tries by rank, each a group set down where nothing is within gap: one big piece (big: [kit/model, weight, [smallest, largest] scale]), medium_n medium things within medium_r of it, small_n small ones within small_r; every piece passes the same tests as the rest. bailey: the castle's yard dressed (dressing.gd; Mac: no bare lawn inside the walls): rows [kit/model, across, toward the gate (shares of the castle's footprint from its middle), turn (degrees), scale]: the training yard (dummies, weapon racks, a shield target) on the gate's left, the stores (barrels, a barrel rack, crates, sacks) and a wagon on its right, the smith's corner (anvil, buckets, chain) by the keep, banners by the gate and the keep, a horse trough with its hitching rail against the wall by the stables corner, where the grooms lead the horses (yard: props/yard, CC0 and CC-BY models with their license.txt).",
